    Zero-shot evaluation of Evo2 model 724
  </heading>
  <list>
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="119"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="125"/>
<![CDATA[All zero-shot tasks were also benchmarked using the Evo2  19 model ('evo2_7b') for comparison. 725]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="131"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="137"/>
    Since Evo2 is autoregressive (predicting the next token rather than masked tokens), masked 726
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="143"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="150"/>
    token accuracy could not be directly computed. Therefore, for the evolutionary constraint task, we 727
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="156"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="162"/>
    fed the full input sequence into the model and extracted the likelihood of the reference allele at 728
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="168"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="174"/>
    the target site as the conservation score. To ensure a fair comparison, we used an 8,192 bp 729
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="180"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="186"/>
    context window for Evo2, matching the input length used for PlantCAD2 evaluations. The same 730
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="192"/>
    <location value="304"/>
    <location value="199"/>
    approach was applied for benchmarking structural variants. 731
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="212"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="219"/>
    For the masked motif accuracy task, we evaluated Evo2 using two configurations to compensate 732
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="225"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="231"/>
    for  its  unidirectional  architecture:  (1)  forward  sequences  (Evo2-fwd),  where  the  model  uses 733
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="237"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="243"/>
    upstream context to predict the junction -for example, for TIS prediction, we used the 4,094 bp 734
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="249"/>
    <location value="452"/>
    <location value="256"/>
    upstream of the TIS as a prompt for Evo2 to generate the next three tokens; and (2) reverse735
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="261"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="268"/>
    complement  sequences  (Evo2-rc),  where  the  model  uses  downstream  context  (reverse 736
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="274"/>
    <location value="319"/>
    <location value="280"/>
    complemented) to predict the junction in the opposite direction. 737
  </list>
